946:- keep route-switch trigger, fallback outcome, and re-prioritization verdict linked to stable `scenario_id`, `run_id`, `cohort_id`, `trace_id`, and `artifact_version` when repeated route behavior is being compared
947:- do not let `Route re-prioritization audit memo` imply benchmarked route quality unless the stronger verdict surface exists
948:- if route-switch evidence is thin, keep the recommendation advisory rather than benchmark-grade
949:- keep `route-switch failure`, `late clarification`, and `failed fallback timing` independently visible when route-quality failure diagnosis is the real issue
950:- let a newer compatible route artifact supersede a stale predecessor explicitly rather than keeping both active
951:- before joining route artifacts, check precedence, compatibility, freshness, and completeness; reject incompatible merges that would weaken the stronger timing verdict
952:- preserve upstream source IDs and `artifact_version` in any joined route artifact that survives benchmark review
